# Design system consumption hierarchy

When building any UI in this app, prefer the highest layer that works. Do not start at primitives.

## 1. Components first

Use published design-system components (`JzButton`, `JzText`, `JzIcon`, etc. from `@jobzeug/design-system/react`) before hand-rolling markup or styles for the same job.

- Prefer component props (`variant`, `color`, `size`, `label`, `level`) over custom CSS that reimplements them.
- Do not recreate buttons, text styles, or icons with raw HTML + tokens when a component already covers it.

## 2. Semantic tokens second

If you need raw CSS (layout shells, gaps, surfaces the components do not own), use **semantic** tokens (`--jz-semantic-*` / `vars["semantic.*"]`).

Pick the right semantic layer for the job:

- **Background / surface**: canvas, surface, control — e.g. `--jz-semantic-color-background-canvas-default`, `…-surface-default`, `…-control-default`
- **Text**: `--jz-semantic-color-text-*` (default, secondary, muted, inverse, error, …) — prefer `JzText` `color` when possible
- **Border, space, type**: semantic border / gap / padding / type tokens

These follow `data-mode` (light / dark / subtle / emphasized). Mode-aware UI must stay on semantics.

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
background: var(--jz-semantic-color-background-canvas-default);
color: var(--jz-semantic-color-text-secondary);
gap: var(--jz-semantic-space-gap-md);
```

## 3. Primitives last (rare)

Use **primitive** tokens (`--jz-primitive-*` / `vars["primitive.*"]`) only when no component and no semantic token fits — e.g. a one-off radius or elevation with no semantic alias.

Primitives are mode-blind raw values. Prefer them almost never; if you reach for one, pause and check for a semantic equivalent first.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — skip semantics */
background: var(--jz-primitive-color-gray-100);

/* ✅ OK only when no semantic exists */
border-radius: var(--jz-primitive-radius-sm);
```

## Quick check

1. Is there a `Jz*` component? → use it  
2. Else, is there a semantic token (surface / text / space / border)? → use it  
3. Else → primitive, sparingly
